# Prism Page Redesign Completion Plan

The goal is to complete the Prism page (`/prism`) redesign based on the Figma reference and the feasibility document. 

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Transparent Navigation Bar
Currently, the navbar on `prism.astro` is set to `bg-[#161616]`. We'll update the `HomeLayout` props in `prism.astro` to make the navbar transparent and blend cleanly with the hero video. We will change:
- `customNavBG` to `bg-transparent`
- `customNavMainBG` to `bg-transparent`

### 2. Chromatic Aberration Effect
We will add a reusable CSS utility for the chromatic aberration glitch effect and apply it to the main hero tagline (`"One Library. Every Connector on Earth."`) and optionally the brand proof heading.
- Create `.glitch-text` class with multi-layered text shadows with slight offsets in cyan, magenta, and yellow/red to match the new Figma aesthetic.

### 3. "Switch Processors" Section (NEW)
We will implement the missing "Switch Processors" section according to the Figma direction.
- **Layout**: Center-aligned heading and subheading, followed by a product visual/placeholder.
- **Background Details**: Dark gray/black background with a combination of `feTurbulence` noise mask and large blurred color blobs (radial-gradients) to give it a modern dark-mode aesthetic.

### 4. Code Integration / Stats Tweaks
- Ensure the Stats section uses the new typography scaling and structure.
- Review spacing to ensure it gracefully handles the missing `prismCrystal` if it falls back.

### 5. Clean up unused assets
We will remove large unneeded assets:
- `src/assets/Prism/prism-hero-bg.svg` (58 KB)
- `src/assets/Prism/prism-hero-visual.svg` (1.1 MB)

## User Review Required
